**Read:** Finish the corrosion sequence and the complete relevant books, reviews and primary methods. Work the three investigations below: electrochemical/environment-assisted damage, polymer aging and service-life inference, and mineral/ceramic deterioration under coupled conditions.

Each investigation begins with a specified material history, function and exposure. Derive a mechanistic account, reconstruct the measurement method, independently check calculations and compare a condition not used for fitting. Use observations to distinguish competing explanations rather than treating a successful curve fit as completion.

**Deliver:** Three substantial studies with traceable sources, equations and units, uncertainty, changed-condition predictions and criticism. Distinguish published measurements from experiments you actually performed and from hypothetical calculations. If source data are missing, explain what can be reconstructed and limit the result. Compare what transfers between the three studies and what depends on the particular material and environment.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
**Continue in materials engineering:** [Advanced study of corrosion and environment-assisted damage](Advanced-study-of-corrosion-and-environment-assisted-damage.lingua#r_3Q6JGQDMQP0ZN4MMMK49DJBM9D), [Advanced study of polymer aging and outdoor life](Advanced-study-of-polymer-aging-and-outdoor-life.lingua#r_7JFQVSY2PPPC6G6AYVVNWECSSQ), [Advanced study of glass, ceramic or cement durability](Advanced-study-of-glass-ceramic-or-cement-durability.lingua#r_1BPHNSVDZ6E72DGA4SKYEBFE47).

